**corollary 20.6 (TBN infinite odd-depth support).** There are infinitely many distinct split primes p with odd h_p, p=3 modulo4, and rho(p)=2*3^s for some s>=2. Within this restricted set, either infinitely many have h_p=1 or infinitely many have odd h_p>=3, or both. At least J distinct primes of those two types combined are at most B_J.

